{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/117913-werewolf-the-forsaken-left-alone","id":117913,"title":"Werewolf The Forsaken left alone :(","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-23T02:57:02-07:00","id":117913,"title":"Werewolf The Forsaken left alone :(","content":"I have a serious problem with books count regarding W:TF. Why there is less books published for W:TF compared to M:TAw or V:TR ? It was the second line that was created by White Wolf in the old times and it is the second line created in the NWoD but what is wrong? People donn't like W:TF ? ( i always wanted to see a Gift List that upgrades Gauru form for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2742-mortisnotrem","name":"Mortisnotrem","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T03:28:47-07:00","id":117920,"title":"","content":"Open Development of Werewolf: the Forsaken<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: The Forsaken &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's getting updated.<br /> <br /> There was a big long thread on the old white wolf forums about the who/what/where/why/hows/etc. of werewolf being unpopular, I know that thread had many many pages, perhaps someone can dig it up for you to peruse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T10:36:06-07:00","id":117987,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think it has everything to do with the developer, Ethan Skemp. That man is just too damn good at his job.<br /> <br /> He developed 2 lines for the NWOD, <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> and <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>. Both seem to have fewer books for the same reason: every book produced is clear, concise and packed to the seams with useful information. Despite the overwhelming success of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>, it still has very few books. There just wasn't a lot of other material that needed to be covered. If you look at the forum for <b>C:tL</b>, most of the discussion is not asking for explanation/expansion on the material, just clarifying what is where, ideas for what kind of game to run and <i>fans </i>expanding on what they have (mostly new Contracts and Entitlements).<br /> <br /> Now, sadly, you don't get that over on the <b>W:tF</b> forum, but that's because the exception to my above statement is that the corebook for the game lacks that clear and concise presentation. I think they were just trying to stuff too much in at once and didn't quite know how to get it all in there. By the time <b>C:tL</b> came along, they figured it out. Myself and a host of other fans are hoping the Idigam Chronicles will fix that problem.<br /> <br /> As far as reading what's already been posted about it,<a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulteb51.html?g=topics&amp;f=12\" target=\"_blank\"> start here on the old forums</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T11:44:45-07:00","id":118023,"title":"","content":"Ehhh... There are a ton of things left in Werewolf the Forsaken that could have been done. And comparing it to Changeling is a strawman - changeling was intended, from the first, to be a limited run game line. Werewolf was not. And, as for Ethan Skimp? Take a look at Geist, which is actively in dire need of updates and new books, but hasn't had any.<br /> <br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is unknown. We don't have access to sales figures or any kind of survey. We don't know if it comes down to something as simple as less book pitches for Werewolf from the small pool of writers we have in the company, who tend to be busy with lots of other labors of love. Everything we could say would be groundless guessing or fanboy love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T11:58:40-07:00","id":118034,"title":"","content":"I don't think it sold as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:10:09-07:00","id":118040,"title":"","content":"Ethan Skemp, not &quot;Skimp&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolf didn't sell as well as the other games. In a way, the fanbase is to blame for the game line receiving less support than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T03:24:18-07:00","id":118365,"title":"","content":"&quot;Blame&quot; is a strong word. And going by DriveThru medals Werewolf sells <i>fine</i> - better than most rpgs on the online market. Just not quite as much as Vampire, Mage, or Changeling. But there's no shame in that, and we love the game. If we only made books for our best-sellers, it would be wall-to-wall V20 and Exalted.<br /> <br /> Production slowed down for a long while - production slowed down for all the nWoD games for a long while, but it happened to Forsaken earlier - but the game has a line developer again, the new corebook is between drafts, and resources are being spent to make it as good as possible.<br /> <br /> When Stew set up the Idigam Chronicle project, he had to fend off writers wanting to get in on it with a stick. That's not a game no one loves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T12:22:05-07:00","id":119225,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty successful game, actually. It's not the best-selling nWoD game, but it's no slouch. And <i>The Idigam Chronicle</i> should be pretty excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T12:26:12-07:00","id":119228,"title":"","content":"Thanks for those words Rose and Dave. They bring hope to my heart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:21:20-07:00","id":124100,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It really helped me to hope for this lovely game again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2742-mortisnotrem","name":"Mortisnotrem","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}